            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0413" n="99" xml:id="pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/20</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-09-07T19:00:00+00:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 7, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10:50 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>621. The agreement between the Allies published to-day that no one will consent
                    to end hostilities till all three consent is England’s declaration to the Kaiser
                    that no peace proposals will be entertained till one side or the other is
                    completely exhausted. The English are preparing for a long war. They mean to
                    fight till promilitarism is utterly crushed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
